<title>NORWAY: Norway's June CPI rises 0.3 pct mnth/mnth.</title>
<headline>Norway's June CPI rises 0.3 pct mnth/mnth.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Statistics Norway (SSB) issued the following economic indicator.</p>
<p>NORWAY CONSUMER PRICES     JUNE 1997   MAY 1997   JUNE 1996</p>
<p>Figures (in percent)</p>
<p>  Month-on-month change	+0.3	 +0.3	  +0.4</p>
<p>  Year-on-year change	  +2.9	 +2.7	  +1.3</p>
<p>  Index (base 1979)	   270.4	269.7	 263.9</p>
<p>NOTE -- Ten economists polled by Reuters had forecast a year-on-year rise in June of 2.7 percent and an increase of 0.1 percent from May.</p>
<p>SSB attributed the rise in inflation to increased property rents and to higher prices for hotels, charter holiday tours and holiday homes. However, gasoline and clothes prices fell, SSB said.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom +47 22 42 50 41</p>
